{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788975789,"nonce":"ejGUuOtGI+LeqiRws4Hzs/VCIHk=","title":"Own the Cranelift backend: implement beadie::JitBackend directly","message":"beadie-cranelift is a reference implementation, not a dependency -- neither\nrayzor (`BeadieJit`) nor zyntax (`ZyntaxCraneliftBackend`) uses its concrete\nbackend. `AshCraneliftBackend` should own its own\n`Arc\u003cMutex\u003ccranelift_jit::JITModule\u003e\u003e` and `FunctionDef`, depending only on the\ncranelift-agnostic `beadie-core` / `beadie-backend` traits.\n\nThis also frees ash to pick its own cranelift version: while ash consumes\nbeadie-cranelift's `CraneliftFunctionDef`, both crates must resolve to the same\ncranelift or the `ir::Function` types are distinct.","files":null}]}